WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.430
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:04.100
You've been shot five
times for your country,

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.700
and you can't even afford to
send your kids to college.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.560
We finally get to use our
skills for our own benefit.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.730
All right, let's do it.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:14.730
(upbeat rock music)

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:18.450
People describe seeing an entity

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.580
that takes on a form of your worst fears.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.413
Oh my god.

00:00:21.413 --> 00:00:22.246
What are you looking at?

00:00:22.246 --> 00:00:23.079
What did you see?

00:00:23.079 --> 00:00:24.130
We're going on the trip now.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.600
It's going to be rough.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.430
But under no circumstance are you

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.790
allowed to take off your blindfold.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:33.930
Every contact we've had with the outside

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.130
has brought us death.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.810
Everybody has a dark side,

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.109
some of us are better at
hiding it than others.

00:00:40.109 --> 00:00:42.070
Oh, martini time.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:43.590
I'm sure it's five o'clock somewhere.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:44.730
Oh my god, did you just come up

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:45.860
with that cliche all by yourself?

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.390
He's such a brilliant man.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.150
I mean I've played through some of these

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:50.480
emergencies before,

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.873
and she disappears for quite some time.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.600
My god, you're such a nerd.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.970
I study the marriage of space and time.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:00.520
You don't realize what lies ahead.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.130
This is going to be a very heavy feat.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.650
We're going to fight this mess together.

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.640
My name is Stephen Hawking.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.190
One never knows where the next

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:12.113
great leap forward is going to come.

00:01:13.044 --> 00:01:16.377
(dramatic techno music)

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.190
This place is real isn't it?

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:32.288
We were born by a sort
of chemical madness.

00:01:32.288 --> 00:01:33.995
A willingness of the heart

00:01:33.995 --> 00:01:36.995
that burst thunderously upon us all.

00:01:37.919 --> 00:01:41.240
Are you wanta sit on
the sidelines and watch,

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.073
or do ya want to play ball?

00:01:42.073 --> 00:01:43.423
Play ball

00:01:43.423 --> 00:01:45.304
Is it good enough for ya?

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:49.163
We don't do what we love
then we wouldn't exist.

00:01:50.099 --> 00:01:51.377
Time kid.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:54.360
Viktor Drago, son of Ivan Drago,

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.740
who infamously killed Apollo Creed,

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.691
appeared today to issue a challenge.

00:01:58.691 --> 00:02:01.507
Now you know what you're fighting for.

00:02:01.507 --> 00:02:03.742
First things first,

00:02:03.742 --> 00:02:05.230
any man here that wants to walk away

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:07.277
can do so knowing their the best of us.

00:02:07.277 --> 00:02:08.700
But it's gotta be now.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.860
You cannot go back to your
normal life after tonight.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.040
You guys need to own the fact that

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.085
what we're about to do is criminal.

00:02:15.085 --> 00:02:16.720
(laughing)

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.200
If we wanted something we just took it.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.530
If anyone complained twice

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.550
they got hit so bad believe me
they never complained again.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:26.720
Murder was the only way that
everybody stayed in line.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.380
You got out of line you got wacked.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.633
Everybody knew the rules.

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:32.733
(plane engine roaring)

00:02:32.733 --> 00:02:34.436
(glass breaking)

00:02:34.436 --> 00:02:35.370
Hey look I don't want to sell it to you.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.270
Its too ugly for that.

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:39.403
When your fighting in your own back yard,

00:02:39.403 --> 00:02:41.063
your fighting for your family.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:45.110
And for them this is just some place,

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:47.737
but for us, this is our home.

00:02:47.737 --> 00:02:49.908
Peter Pans gots kids.

00:02:49.908 --> 00:02:51.491
Jesse James Hook.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.190
Fueling spawn, how I despise them.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:57.573
What do you want old man?

00:02:57.573 --> 00:02:58.633
Just you.

00:02:59.835 --> 00:03:03.450
You need a mother very very badly.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.623
Daughter, the path will not be easy.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:10.580
The world outside is lifeless.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.650
But I made you into the woman that you are

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:15.010
so that we could do this together.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.420
This facility was designed

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.990
to give humanity a second chance.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.370
There's a droid here.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:23.480
Their guest has not been
entirely truthful with us.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.870
Your whole life I've taught
you to see the bigger picture.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:29.083
Everything I do is to protect you.

00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:31.930
Suru, my beautiful boy.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:33.123
I had another family.

00:03:33.123 --> 00:03:34.121
What happened?

00:03:34.121 --> 00:03:36.165
(mumbles)

00:03:36.165 --> 00:03:36.998
I was lost.

00:03:36.998 --> 00:03:38.979
(train whistly blowing)

00:03:38.979 --> 00:03:40.990
I have to find my way back home.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.756
What if you do find home
and their not even there?

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:44.963
And you just keep searching.

00:03:44.963 --> 00:03:46.925
I'm going on an adventure.

00:03:46.925 --> 00:03:51.685
True courage is about knowing
not when to take a life,

00:03:51.685 --> 00:03:53.180
but when to spare one.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.513
I've never been so wrong in all my life.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.940
I don't understand what
their doing in my house!

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:02.107
(upbeat guitar music)

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:05.442
Welcome to Baywatch.

00:04:05.442 --> 00:04:08.800
Our team is the elite of the elite.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.970
We're the heart and
soul of this very beach.

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:13.600
Why do she always look like
she's running in slo-mo?

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.690
You see it too?

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.523
I'm Matt Brody.

00:04:15.523 --> 00:04:18.320
This is the guy you think is
a good PR opportunity for us.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:19.153
Give me some shots!

00:04:19.153 --> 00:04:20.881
I'm ready to party.

00:04:24.233 --> 00:04:26.480
Will you be my maid of honor?

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:27.420
Of course I will!

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.510
Let's go meet the rest
of the bridal party.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:30.767
You must be Annie's fella?

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:31.600
I'm not.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:32.433
He's not.

00:04:32.433 --> 00:04:33.266
I'm not with him.

00:04:33.266 --> 00:04:34.099
I'm glad he's single cause

00:04:34.099 --> 00:04:36.020
I'm gonna climb that like a tree.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:37.870
You better hold on tight spider monkey.

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:39.556
I'm not scared of you.

00:04:39.556 --> 00:04:41.533
Well you really shouldn't have said that.

00:04:41.533 --> 00:04:43.003
This isn't real.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.090
This kind of stuff just doesn't exist.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.744
It does in my world.

00:04:47.744 --> 00:04:50.620
(gun shots firing)

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:51.617
Let's do our thing.

00:04:51.617 --> 00:04:53.363
And the name is Shaft.

00:04:53.363 --> 00:04:54.988
(glass breaking)

00:04:54.988 --> 00:04:56.080
Yeah!

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.200
Oh!

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:58.700
John Shaft.

00:04:58.700 --> 00:04:59.800
What are you doing?

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:00.875
I'm done workin for the man.

00:05:00.875 --> 00:05:01.960
Ah

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.826
Junior get in the car.

00:05:03.826 --> 00:05:04.659
Now.

00:05:06.833 --> 00:05:07.843
Boom.

00:05:07.843 --> 00:05:08.676
Ah!

00:05:08.676 --> 00:05:09.520
It's just like Death in a Library.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:11.680
What happens in Death in a Library?

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:12.660
They died.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.056
That's why its called Death in a Library.

00:05:14.056 --> 00:05:15.054
Ah.

00:05:15.054 --> 00:05:16.389
(mumbles)

00:05:16.389 --> 00:05:19.489
(car engine revving)

00:05:19.489 --> 00:05:22.017
(glass breaking)

00:05:22.017 --> 00:05:22.850
I didn't do it.

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:25.330
Of course you didn't
do it, you little twit.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:26.340
Now you all remember

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:28.270
how scary your first days at school were.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:30.990
You wanted cake you got cake.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:32.400
Now eat it!

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:33.950
I'm fed up with all this reading.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:34.783
Your a Wormwood.

00:05:34.783 --> 00:05:36.205
You start acting like one.

00:05:36.205 --> 00:05:39.288
(upbeat rock music)

